[user-comment] Title: Desktop (explorer.exe): taps on Start button never reach it; clicks land on child-desktop window 0x1004c  Build: BCD v0.1.626 (626) Device: iPhone13,4, iOS 18.6.2 (22G100), 5.7 GB RAM Game/profile: Desktop (explorer.exe), 1280x720, mode=fit Input: aim mode "right", sensitivity 1.0, "tap clicks", layout "PC keyboard"  Problem Tapping the Start button with the touch trackpad does nothing, no matter how many times I try. It used to work when the mouse cursor icon was small. After the cursor became bigger, it stopped working. (I can't confirm from the log that cursor size is the cause.)  Steps to reproduce 1. Open Desktop from the library. 2. Move the cursor over the Start button (bottom-left). 3. Tap to click. The Start menu does not open.  Evidence from explorer_exe-2026-11-01_17-38-15.txt - Taskbar: Shell_TrayWnd 0x30030 win={0,700,1280,720} - Start button: Button 0x1003c win={0,700,56,720} - Clicks do reach wineserver, e.g.   [srv-input] btn msg=0x201 at (33,706) hit win=0001004c thread=0x0   Other points: (9,708), (13,708), (27,714), (36,712), (41,709), (50,708). All are inside the Start button rect. - Every click hit win=0001004c (thread=0x0). None hit 0x1003c or Shell_TrayWnd. - 0x1004c is the top_window created by (line 2696):   err:win:ios_child_desktop_fixup [child-desktop] pid=0054 ... no desktop window (status 0xc0000008, thread desktop 0x8) ... top_window=0x1004c msg_window=0x1004e - One click at (58,725) is outside the button and the 720px screen. - [hwinput] minute lines show buttons=0, mice=0, cursor=hidden. Two of them show route=blocked right after the app returned from inactive. - Also an error: Session log: could not link logs/explorer.exe-...txt ("bcd-log.txt" couldn't be linked to "logs" because an item with the same name already exists.)  Expected: the click is delivered to Start button 0x1003c and the menu opens. Actual: the click is delivered to the child process desktop window 0x1004c, so the Start button never gets it.  S
